{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And we will cover his blood</b> — and we will conceal his death; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 37:26). And Onkelos likewise said (Onkelos on Genesis 37:26) \"ונכסי על דמיה\" (and we will cover his blood). But the correct interpretation is the plain sense, for the practice of those who kill in secret is to kill the victim and bury him and cover his blood with earth, as it says (Exodus 2:12) \"and he hid him in the sand.\" And therefore he said to them: Behold, we are killing our brother and covering his blood with earth, for thus it will be accounted to us. And behold, Reuben taught them that they should not shed blood directly, but rather cast him into the pit and let him die there, for the punishment of one who causes death is not like the punishment of one who sheds blood. And now Judah came and said: even this will be accounted to us as murder, as though we ourselves killed him — and so the matter is in truth, as in that which Scripture says (II Samuel 12:9) \"and him you killed by the sword of the children of Ammon.\" But there is a great law and a small law between them (i.e., a distinction in severity), and both of them spoke truth."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:08.391487469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}